A multi-line text field that shares [Input](<%= page_path(:input) %>)'s look, variants, sizes and slots.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/textarea)

<%= embed AppicaUI::TextareaPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Textarea(rows: 4, placeholder: "Write a message…", aria_label: "Message")
Textarea(value: @post.body, name: "post[body]", clearable: true)
Textarea(start_slot: -> { Avatar(size: :"2xs") { AvatarImage(src: user.avatar_url) } },
         end_slot: -> { Button(variant: :soft, size: :sm, icon: true) { Icon(:send_2) } })
```

`rows:` sets the starting height; the user can still resize it vertically. `value:` is the content. Slots align to
the first line of text; with a slot or `clearable:` the textarea sits in a frame that `class:` styles, and
`textarea: { … }` reaches the inner element.

